  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: I have a single RNA-only baseline (config_015: singleprofile, scgpt → acc 0.411, F1 0.378). The most critical open question is whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal at all. Without an image-only baseline, any future multimodal result would be uninterpretable—improvement could come from image information, from multiprofile/aggregation machinery, or from both. 2) What this tests: config_041 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation, no fusion) isolates the contribution of the image modality under the same simplicity constraints as the RNA baseline (single profile, no aggregation, no fusion). It directly answers: 'Does image data alone provide comparable or complementary signal to RNA?' 3) Why it is the best use of the next experiment: It is the single most informative experiment to reduce uncertainty about the fundamental design decision (include image or not). It changes only the modality relative to config_015 while holding profile setting, aggregation, and fusion constant, giving a clean unimodal-to-unimodal comparison. This baseline is a prerequisite for interpreting any subsequent multimodal or multiprofile experiment, making it the highest-value next step under a limited budget."
}

